# Changelog

All notable changes to the SPC Real-Time Monitoring System.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),
and this project follows semantic versioning at a high level.

---

## [2.0] — 2026-04 — Camera vs CMM Correlation Release

This release closes the loop on the original 2023 stakeholder requirement:
**validating camera measurements against CMM**. v1.0 delivered centralization
and real-time monitoring; v2.0 brings CMM data into the same database and
builds the analytical layer to compare the two.

### Added — Data Integration

- **CMM data pipeline via Microsoft Power Platform**
  - Power App form for worker submissions (irregular timing, mobile-friendly)
  - Excel staging file for intermediate storage
  - Power Automate flow for extract + transform
  - SQL Gateway bridging cloud to on-prem SQL Server
  - CMM data lands in the same `spc_database` as camera data, enabling joins
  - Scope: I designed up to the SQL staging layer; final ingestion handoff
    handled by a separate team

### Added — Visualization

- **4-page Power BI dashboard** (replaces v1.0 single-page report)
  - Page 1: Daily PPK summary with donut chart + Pareto chart, line and
    data-source filters
  - Page 2: Drill-down line chart of XYZ contributions to GD&T, with
    temperature overlay
  - Page 3: Camera vs CMM gap analysis on shared measurement points
  - Page 4: Camera vs CMM correlation scatter plot with trend line

### Added — Database

**Camera-side statistics tables:**
- **`spc_gdt_stats`** table — full SPC snapshot with foreign key
  (`gdt_data_id`) back to source measurement row in `spc_gdt`
- **`spc_xyz_stats`** table — same design, FK `xyz_data_id` to `spc_xyz`
- Both tables include: `window_size`, `sample_count`, `rolling_mean`,
  `rolling_stdev`, `UCL`, `LCL`, `PPU`, `PPL`, `PPK`, `PP`, `ppk_status`,
  `calculated_at`

**CMM table set (mirror of Camera structure):**
- **`cmm_header`** — CMM submission metadata (mirrors `spc_header`)
- **`cmm_gdt`** — CMM GD&T measurements (mirrors `spc_gdt`)
- **`cmm_xyz`** — CMM XYZ measurements (mirrors `spc_xyz`)
- **`cmm_specs`** — CMM specs (mirrors `spc_specs` + `camera_mapping` column)
- **`cmm_gdt_stats`** — CMM GDT statistics with lineage (mirrors `spc_gdt_stats`)
- **`cmm_xyz_stats`** — CMM XYZ statistics with lineage (mirrors `spc_xyz_stats`)

**Spec table column extensions (both `spc_specs` and `cmm_specs`):**
- **`xyz_axis`** column on specs — `"X"`, `"Y"`, `"Z"` for XYZ points;
  `"None"` for GD&T points (calculated values, no single axis)
- **`gdt_xyz_link`** column — maps each GD&T point to the XYZ points used
  to calculate it; enables drill-down from GD&T PPK to component XYZ
  measurements

**CMM-specific spec column:**
- **`camera_mapping`** column on `cmm_specs` only — maps each CMM
  measurement code to its equivalent Camera measurement code; this is
  the join key for Camera vs CMM correlation queries (Pages 3 & 4)

**Data table change:**
- **`xyz_axis`** is now a dedicated column on `spc_xyz` / `cmm_xyz` /
  `spc_xyz_stats` / `cmm_xyz_stats` (was a suffix in `data_type` in v1.0)

### Added — Code

- **`statistics_calculator.py`** module — replaces v1.0 `unified_ppk_calculator.py`
  - Per-run calculation with `calculate_for_run()` entry point
  - Rolling 125-sample window using `TOP() ORDER BY DESC` SQL pattern
  - One-sided spec handling (PPU-only or PPL-only) — fixes v1 NULL bug
  - PPK capability classification: Capable (≥1.33) / Marginal (≥1.00) /
    Not Capable, with "(Low Sample)" suffix when n < 125
  - Debug counters: `ppk_calculated`, `ppk_skipped_no_spec`,
    `ppk_skipped_no_data`, `ppk_skipped_std_zero`
  - Auto-creates statistics tables if they don't exist
  - Duplicate-check via LIKE pattern on base run_number

- **PySpark JDBC option in `spec_loader.py`**
  - Primary path: PySpark JDBC for bulk spec read
  - Automatic fallback: pyodbc if PySpark unavailable or fails
  - Same Excel cache layer regardless of read path

- **Auto-reconnect logic** in main scripts
  - Health-check via `SELECT 1` before each cycle
  - Up to 3 retry attempts with 10-second delay
  - Fully closes dead connection before reconnecting
  - 60-second backoff if all retries fail

- **Statistics retry queue**
  - Failed stats calculations are added to `stats_failed_runs[]`
  - Retried at end of scan cycle
  - Prevents losing PPK data when SQL has transient issues

- **Post-insert verification** (`verify_sql_insert()`)
  - Counts rows in all 7 tables for each run
  - Flags MISSING tables for visibility into partial failures
  - Logs OK / MISSING per table

- **Line_R production line support**
  - Different Excel layout: 275 GDT rows, 470 XYZ rows
  - Different filename pattern
  - Different cell mappings for status, temperature, model

- **UTF-8 console reconfiguration** for Windows
  - `sys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding='utf-8', errors='replace')`
  - Fixes UnicodeEncodeError on Windows console

### Changed

- `xyz_axis` is no longer encoded in `data_type` string
  - v1: `data_type = "LH X" / "LH Y" / "LH Z" / "RH X" / ...`
  - v2: `data_type = "LH" / "RH"`, `xyz_axis = "X" / "Y" / "Z" / "N"`
- Spec dictionary lookup uses composite key `{measurement_code}_{side}`
- Blank `point_group` in `spc_specs` now creates shared LH/RH specs (was
  ambiguous in v1.0)
- Statistics calculation moved from per-cycle batch to per-run immediate
  - Faster reflection in dashboards
  - Each run gets its own statistics snapshot with lineage

### Fixed

- **PPK = NULL when one spec limit was zero**
  - Root cause: v1 only calculated PPK when both `spec_min` and `spec_max`
    were non-NULL
  - Fix: handle one-sided specs (e.g., flatness with `spec_min = 0`)
  - PP also fixed to handle one-sided correctly
- **Statistics lost on database connection drops mid-cycle**
  - Now caught and retried at end of cycle
- **Silent partial inserts**
  - When one of 5 (now 7) tables silently failed, no detection in v1
  - v2 verification catches and logs this
- **Duplicate statistics calculation**
  - LIKE pattern on `run_number_base` prevents double-insert when stats
    are recalculated

### Internal Notes

- Database schema is **backward compatible** — all v1 tables unchanged;
  spec column additions (`xyz_axis`, `gdt_xyz_link`) are nullable
- v1.0 main scripts can run against v2.0 database without modification
- v2.0 main scripts read v1.0 historical data correctly
- Migration: drop v1's `unified_ppk_calculator.py`, deploy v2's
  `statistics_calculator.py`, restart services per line
- New CMM tables can be created independently — they don't affect any
  Camera-side code

### Architecture Decisions Recorded (v2.0)

- **Mirror tables for CMM, not merged tables** — chose `cmm_*` tables that
  parallel `spc_*` tables instead of a shared schema with a `data_source`
  discriminator column. Reasons: different volumes (per-product vs sampled),
  different ingestion paths (Python file watcher vs Power Platform),
  different point counts (CMM has extra accuracy points), and clean
  failure isolation.
- **Spec table as bridge layer** — chose to put the CMM-to-Camera mapping
  on `cmm_specs.camera_mapping` rather than a separate junction table.
  This keeps the mapping versionable with `is_active`, queryable as a
  lookup dimension, and avoids extra joins in correlation queries.
- **`xyz_axis` extended to spec tables** — chose to denormalize this
  attribute onto specs (with `"None"` for GD&T) so axis-based filters
  can run against specs alone without joining to data tables.
- **`gdt_xyz_link` for traceability** — chose to record GD&T → XYZ
  relationships explicitly in specs rather than parsing measurement codes
  at query time. This makes Page 2 drill-down queries simple and fast.
- **Power Platform for CMM ingestion** — chose Power App + Power Automate
  + SQL Gateway over a Python script because the data source is human
  worker submission on irregular timing. Workers need a form, not a
  script trigger.
- **Per-run statistics calculation** (vs v1's per-batch) — chose
  immediate calculation per run for fresher dashboard data and simpler
  retry semantics.

---

## [1.0] — 2025-12 — Initial Production Release

The first production release. Solved the centralization and real-time
monitoring requirements from the 2023 stakeholder ask.

### Added

- **Excel-to-SQL ETL pipeline** for camera inspection data
  - Auto-scan source folder, regex filename validation
  - Read GD&T sheet (LH + RH columns)
  - Read XYZ data sheet (LH + RH columns)
  - Read metadata sheet (temperature, model type, status)
  - Two-phase insert: raw measurements + SPC snapshot

- **5 universal database tables**
  - `spc_header` — file metadata, run number, status
  - `spc_gdt` — GD&T measurements + UCL/LCL records
  - `spc_xyz` — XYZ coordinate measurements + UCL/LCL records
  - `spc_ppk` — PPK/PP calculation results (legacy)
  - `spc_specs` — specification limits per line per point

- **PPK / PP / UCL / LCL calculation engine** (`unified_ppk_calculator.py`)
  - Rolling 125-sample window
  - Two-sided spec calculations
  - UCL / LCL clamping to spec limits for display

- **Spec loading with Excel cache** (`spec_loader.py`)
  - First load: query SQL `spc_specs` table via pyodbc
  - Save to Excel cache for fast subsequent loads
  - Manual refresh by deleting cache file

- **Multi-line support**
  - Universal schema (`production_line` column separates lines)
  - Per-line main script with line-specific DATA_MAP
  - Initially supported: Line_01, Line_02

- **Visualization integrations**
  - Grafana dashboards for real-time SPC monitoring
  - Power BI report for weekly/monthly quality analysis

- **Reliability features**
  - Duplicate detection across local log + SQL
  - ODBC driver auto-detection (4 fallback drivers)
  - Shift-based Excel summary reports
  - Activity logging to console + Excel

- **Quality status logic**
  - OK / NG / N/A based on spec_min ≤ value ≤ spec_max comparison
  - File-level FG/NG aggregation

### Architecture Decisions Recorded

- **Universal tables over per-line tables** — chose `production_line`
  column approach for simpler dashboard queries and adding new lines
  without schema changes
- **pyodbc with executemany** — chose over SQLAlchemy ORM for raw
  insert performance on high-frequency data
- **Excel cache for specs** — chose over always-query SQL because specs
  change rarely and cache cuts startup time from ~2s to ~0.1s
- **Two-phase insert** — chose to separate raw data insert from SPC
  calculation so file processing doesn't block on PPK math

---

## How to Read This Changelog

- **Added** — new features, capabilities, tables, or modules
- **Changed** — modifications to existing behavior (may affect downstream
  consumers like dashboards or queries)
- **Fixed** — bug fixes
- **Internal Notes** — migration guidance, compatibility notes, scope
  clarifications

For deeper context on any release, see [README.md](README.md).
